        <section id="what-is-coding?"  class="t-bg-primary">
          
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          What is coding?
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <p>Coding is a term used to refer to writing software.</p>
<p>Coding is the process used to make an electronic device do what it needs to do. From a binary level, simply turning on and off, all the way to more advanced coding languages used to create programs. It is the 'language' we use to communicate with computers to enable them to understand what we want them to do and to then process that information. It allows humans to essentially 'talk’ to machines and create computer software like programs, games, operating systems, and mobile apps.</p>
<p>Programming is the process of assembling sequences of 'codes' or instructions arranged in different orders or groupings to complete a process or carry out a task.</p>
<p>The smallest mistake in coding can significantly affect an entire computer program. This is also something that 'hackers' can then take advantage of.</p>

      </div>
          <img class="l-media__img" src="~/images/svg/uc/uc_u1_s1_p3_image.svg" alt="" width="300" height="300" >  
    </div>
