          <toggle-section open="false">
            <h3>Video transcript </h3>
            <p><strong>Leah:</strong> Early computer codes date back to the 19th Century and many modern programming languages stem from 'Ada Lovelace's first machine algorithm' which was developed for Charles Babbage's Difference machine in 1843.</p>
<p>It was the 1940's that the first modern computers were created along with machine-specific assembly language.</p>
<p>However, it was the 1950's that the first modern programming language was born. This was FORTRAN short for formula translator.</p>
<p>Others were to follow such as</p>
<p>LISP - list processor,</p>
<p>ALGOL -algorithmic language</p>
<p>and COBOL -common business-oriented language.</p>
<p>In the 1960's BASIC had been invented and then C was released.</p>
<p>Unix was developed in the 1970’s and it’s code rewritten in ‘C’ in 1972, the first major OS or operating system not in assembly language.</p>
<p>Linux first released in 1991 is written almost entirely in C and both Windows and macOS both contain C.</p>
<p>The 1990’s also welcomed some of today’s most recognisable languages such as Python, Java, Java Script and PHP. Which opened the world to social media, Android/OS apps and streaming services.</p>
<p>To learn more, take a look at the website further down on this page…</p>

