          <toggle-section open="false">
            <h3>Video transcript </h3>
            <p><strong>Jack:</strong> There are many different coding languages used in programming, let’s have a look at some of the more popular ones.</p>
<p><strong>Leah:</strong> Python</p>
<p>Python is an interpreted high-level general-purpose programming language. It is object oriented and used in everything from developing application programming interfaces or API’s, to being incorporated into machine learning and data analytics via third party plug ins like SciPY and Panda. Python has been used to create everything from Netflix's recommendation algorithm to the software that controls self-driving cars.</p>
<p><strong>Jack:</strong> JavaScript</p>
<p>JavaScript often tops the list of the most popular programming languages due to its continuous use in open-source projects. It is a dynamic and interpreted programming language with object-oriented capabilities, that's used for web applications, game development and lots more. It allows for creating dynamic features on web pages that cannot be done with only HTML and CSS.</p>
<p><strong>Leah:</strong> Java</p>
<p>Java is a general purpose, class based, object-oriented programming language designed for application development and has less implementation dependencies. It is secure, fast, and reliable. It is widely used for developing applications in laptops, data centres, games consoles and mobile phones. It is essentially the parent of Java Script and is now mostly associated with game developers. It's an open source and a popular choice for creative coding.</p>
<p><strong>Jack:</strong> C++</p>
<p>C++ is a general-purpose programming language based on the older language C. It is used in one way or another in every complex system in the world from Operating Systems to Government mainframes. Even Google uses this programming language for its most resource intensive operations. Internet of Things [IoT] devices also make use of C++, and it is useful for building complex open-source systems.</p>
<p><strong>Leah:</strong> C#</p>
<p>C# is another object-oriented language commonly used in game developing. A member of the 'C' language family it shares similar logic to C++ but is regarded as easier to use. It is commonly used for Windows applications, and it’s recommended for building games on the ‘Unity’ engine. The language’s specific syntax makes it easy for 3D development, so is good for making VR applications.</p>
<p><strong>Jack:</strong> SQL</p>
<p>SQL stands for Structured Query Language and is used to communicate with a database. For those who wish to work with databases SQL is ideal as it is a very practical language and easy to use and uses a syntax that is similar to English which helps to create a smooth learning curve.</p>
<p><strong>Leah:</strong> Scala</p>
<p>Scala is another popular programming language often seen as an alternative to Java. It is a multi- paradigm general purpose programme, supporting both object oriented and functional programming and can be applied to many areas of development.</p>
<p><strong>Jack:</strong> Ruby</p>
<p>Ruby is regarded as simple to learn and a good starting place for budding developers. It is most often used to build websites and web applications.</p>
<p><strong>Leah:</strong> Swift</p>
<p>Swift is a relatively new language that has a strong following due to the convenience it offers to open-source developers. It is behind most modern iOS applications.</p>
<p><strong>Jack:</strong> PHP</p>
<p>PHP is a programming language mostly used for web development. It is a simple language with logic and syntax that can be mastered quite quickly. It is used for WordPress websites and platforms like Facebook.</p>

